# C's `&&` and `||`: one DS0111 each, with fixes. The tree keeps `and` above `or` precedence.
mode: syntax
---- query
from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 && amount < 100 || customerId == "c-001"
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..79
  PIPELINE@0..78
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    LITERAL@5..17
      STRING@5..17 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
    PIPE@18..19 "|"
    WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
    WHERE_OP@20..78
      IDENT@20..25 "where"
      WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
      BIN_EXPR@26..78
        BIN_EXPR@26..53
          BIN_EXPR@26..37
            NAME_REF@26..32
              IDENT@26..32 "amount"
            WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
            GT@33..34 ">"
            WHITESPACE@34..35 " "
            LITERAL@35..37
              LONG@35..37 "10"
          WHITESPACE@37..38 " "
          AMP2@38..40 "&&"
          WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
          BIN_EXPR@41..53
            NAME_REF@41..47
              IDENT@41..47 "amount"
            WHITESPACE@47..48 " "
            LT@48..49 "<"
            WHITESPACE@49..50 " "
            LITERAL@50..53
              LONG@50..53 "100"
        WHITESPACE@53..54 " "
        PIPE2@54..56 "||"
        WHITESPACE@56..57 " "
        BIN_EXPR@57..78
          NAME_REF@57..67
            IDENT@57..67 "customerId"
          WHITESPACE@67..68 " "
          EQ2@68..70 "=="
          WHITESPACE@70..71 " "
          LITERAL@71..78
            STRING@71..78 "\"c-001\""
  WHITESPACE@78..79 "\n"

error[DS0111]: `&&` is not an operator
  --> query:1:39
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 && amount < 100 || customerId == "c-001"
  |                                       ^^ this is C's "and"
  |
  = help: use `and` to require both conditions: `amount > 10 and amount < 100`

error[DS0111]: `||` is not an operator
  --> query:1:55
  |
1 | from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 && amount < 100 || customerId == "c-001"
  |                                                       ^^ this is C's "or"
  |
  = help: use `or` to accept either condition

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from 'orders.csv' | where amount > 10 and amount < 100 or customerId == "c-001"
which parses without errors
